{"defs":{"0":[{"path":["time:hasTRS"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasTRS","description":"identifier for a temporal reference system; default is million years before prsent as a decimal number","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasTRS"},{"path":["time:numericPosition"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#numericPosition","required":true,"schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#numericPosition"}],"1":[{"path":["time:inXSDDate"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inXSDDate","description":"the date of the instant, as an xsd:date","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inXSDDate"}]},"properties":[{"path":["schema:distribution"],"id":"http://schema.org/distribution","description":"How to access the dataset: file downloads (DataDownload) or API access (WebAPI).","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/distribution"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf"],"sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"keyword":"anyOf"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0"],"title":"a","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","_then"],"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"keyword":"then"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","_else"],"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"keyword":"else"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","description":"Description of this distribution, e.g. what format, access constraints, etc.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:contentUrl"],"id":"http://schema.org/contentUrl","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/contentUrl"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:encodingFormat"],"id":"http://schema.org/encodingFormat","description":"MIME type with extension; should indicate the serialization scheme in sufficient detail that machine can know how to parse.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/encodingFormat"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType"],"id":"http://schema.org/additionalType","description":"Domain-specific type classification for this distribution: what KIND of thing the file is, beyond its MIME type. schema:encodingFormat says how to parse the bytes; this says what they are. A plain string is accepted, but a schema:DefinedTerm carrying schema:inDefinedTermSet is preferred where the value comes from a controlled vocabulary, so the vocabulary travels with the data rather than being asserted only in a profile.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/additionalType"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:contentSize"],"id":"http://schema.org/contentSize","description":"File size of this distribution, e.g. '2.5 MB' or a byte count. Per schema.org/contentSize.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/contentSize"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:width"],"id":"http://schema.org/width","description":"Pixel width of this distribution when it is a single raster file, as a QuantitativeValue. schema:width has schema:MediaObject in its domain. A QuantitativeValue rather than a bare number because the same property carries physical dimensions elsewhere, so the unit has to be stated. (schema:contentSize above is a plain string for historical reasons; that inconsistency is left alone rather than widened.)","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/width"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:width","schema:value"],"id":"http://schema.org/value","description":"Width in pixels.","schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/value"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:width","schema:unitText"],"id":"http://schema.org/unitText","description":"Unit of measure, e.g. 'pixel'.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/unitText"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:height"],"id":"http://schema.org/height","description":"Pixel height of this distribution when it is a single raster file, as a QuantitativeValue. schema:height has schema:MediaObject in its domain. A QuantitativeValue rather than a bare number because the same property carries physical dimensions elsewhere, so the unit has to be stated. (schema:contentSize above is a plain string for historical reasons; that inconsistency is left alone rather than widened.)","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/height"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:height","schema:value"],"id":"http://schema.org/value","description":"Height in pixels.","schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/value"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:height","schema:unitText"],"id":"http://schema.org/unitText","description":"Unit of measure, e.g. 'pixel'.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/unitText"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","spdx:checksum"],"description":"A string value calculated from the content of the resource representation, used to test if content has been modified. The checksum is a property of a particular distribution/DataDownload.","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"]},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","spdx:checksum","spdx:algorithm"],"required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"]},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","spdx:checksum","spdx:checksumValue"],"required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"]},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","dcterms:conformsTo"],"description":"An identifier for a standard or specification that the distribution conforms to. Recommended to enable machine-actionable data access.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"]},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider"],"id":"http://schema.org/provider","description":"Party who maintains this particular distribution option for the dataset. Use this property if there are multiple distributions from different providers","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.dataDownload"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/provider"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1"],"title":"b","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:serviceType"],"id":"http://schema.org/serviceType","description":"specify the kind of service. Ideally this should be a resolvable identifier. Currently there is no widely adopted registry for serviceType identifiers, in large part because services might be defined at different levels of granularity, and classifications might focus on function, data formats, thematic content, security, or other aspects of the service definition. For interoperability, there must be an external arrangement between data providers and consumers on the strings that will be used to specify service types.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.webAPI"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/serviceType"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:termsOfService"],"id":"http://schema.org/termsOfService","description":"Description of access privileges required to use the API, e.g. registration, licensing, payments. Note that access constraints applying to all distributions of the resource should be specified in the access constraints for the resource description as a whole.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.webAPI"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/termsOfService"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:documentation"],"id":"http://schema.org/documentation","description":"a document that provides a machine-actionable description of a service instance. Examples include OpenAPI documents, OGC Capabilities documents. Software designed to utilise a particular service type will typically include functionality to parse such a description document and engage with the service endpoint. If such a document is available for the service instance providing the resource distribution, it should be included in the distribution metadata.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.webAPI"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/documentation"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction"],"id":"http://schema.org/potentialAction","description":"actions that can be invoked via the API","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.webAPI"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/potentialAction"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"text label for the action","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:target"],"id":"http://schema.org/target","description":"specifies the request target location and request syntax. Documentation of the URL end point and syntax to invoke the service. This schema doesn't handle post requests.","required":true,"schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/target"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:target","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:target","schema:urlTemplate"],"id":"http://schema.org/urlTemplate","description":"a templated URL; parameters are enclosed in curly braces ({..}); parameters are not required. If included, parameters MUST be documented in the query-input element. Template should be consitent with URI Template (https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6570) examples: - http://portal.chordsrt.com/api/v1/data.{encoding}; single parameter - http://portal.chordsrt.com/api/v1/data.{encoding}?instruments={instruments}&start={start}&end={end} ; multiple parameters - {endpoint}{encoding}; endpoint URL path is a parameter,should only appear in potential actions for API specification descriptions, which are generic-not specific to a particular endpoint.","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/urlTemplate"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:target","schema:httpMethod"],"id":"http://schema.org/httpMethod","title":"HTTP Method","description":"only applicable if protocol is http or a protocol that tunnels on http","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/httpMethod"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:target","schema:contentType"],"id":"http://schema.org/contentType","description":"The supported content type(s) for an EntryPoint response. a MIME type (https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml) that specifies the content type for messages in resonses from the service endpoint. This is a schema.org property, and is redundant with encodingFormat in the result property for the Action.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/contentType"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:result"],"id":"http://schema.org/result","description":"specifies the serialization scheme (encoding format, information model) for the expected representation of the data - documentation of the serialization format for the API response. See the actionResult building block.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/result"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:result","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"text label for the result/response format.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.actionResult"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:result","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","description":"description of the result/response representation.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.actionResult"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:result","schema:encodingFormat"],"id":"http://schema.org/encodingFormat","description":"MIME type(s) of the response serialization.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.actionResult"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/encodingFormat"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:result","dcterms:conformsTo"],"id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo","description":"identifier(s) for a standard or specification the response conforms to.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.actionResult"],"effectiveId":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:object"],"id":"http://schema.org/object","description":"The entity upon which the action is carried out, whose state is kept intact or changed. This is an open ended class for general description of Actions. When schema:Action (or a subclass) is used to describe operations for a WebAPI distribution, the object is implicitly the resource that is the subject of the containing metadata record, so this property would be superfluous.","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/object"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:object","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:query-input"],"id":"http://schema.org/query-input","description":"set of explanations of the parameters in the URL template for the target.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/query-input"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:query-input","schema:valueName"],"id":"http://schema.org/valueName","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/valueName"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:query-input","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:query-input","schema:valueRequired"],"id":"http://schema.org/valueRequired","schema_type":"boolean","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/valueRequired"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:potentialAction","schema:query-input","schema:valuePattern"],"id":"http://schema.org/valuePattern","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.action"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/valuePattern"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage"],"id":"http://schema.org/spatialCoverage","description":"Geographic area covered by the dataset.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/spatialCoverage"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:additionalType"],"id":"http://schema.org/additionalType","description":"Domain-specific type classifications for this place (e.g. facility type,laboratory classification, feature type).","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/additionalType"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"A place name for the location, either as a string or a DefinedTerm from a gazetteer.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:identifier"],"id":"http://schema.org/identifier","description":"Formal identifier for this place (e.g. ROR identifier for a facility).","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/identifier"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:alternateName"],"id":"http://schema.org/alternateName","description":"Alternate or abbreviated name(s) for this place.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/alternateName"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo"],"id":"http://schema.org/geo","description":"Either a bounding box or a point location.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/geo"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo","_anyOf"],"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"keyword":"anyOf"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo","_anyOf","0"],"title":"a","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo","_anyOf","0","schema:latitude"],"id":"http://schema.org/latitude","required":true,"schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/latitude"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo","_anyOf","0","schema:longitude"],"id":"http://schema.org/longitude","required":true,"schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/longitude"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo","_anyOf","1"],"title":"b","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo","_anyOf","1","schema:box"],"id":"http://schema.org/box","description":"A GeoShape box defines an area on the surface of the earth defined by point locations of the southwest corner and northeast corner of the rectangle in latitude-longitude coordinates. A space should be used to separate the latitude and longitude values. The two corner coordinate points are separated by a space. 'East longitude' means positive longitude values are east of the prime (Greenwich) meridian.","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/box"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo","_anyOf","2"],"title":"c","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","schema:geo","_anyOf","2","schema:line"],"id":"http://schema.org/line","description":"A GeoShape box defines a curvilinear geometry as a string of latitude-longitude coordinates. A space should be used to separate the latitude and longitude values. The coordinate point pairs are also separated by a space. 'East longitude' means positive longitude values are east of the prime (Greenwich) meridian. e.g. '39.33 120.77 40.44 123.96 41.00 121.34' ","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/line"},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","geosparql:hasGeometry"],"description":"Optional geographic extent using wkt geometry, see Ocean InfoHub (https://book.oceaninfohub.org/thematics/spatial/README.html#simple-geosparql-wkt). Other geometry schemes might be specified in a specific domain profile, e.g. for atmospheric, subsurface data, or local coordinate systems. NOTE that the location specified here should be the same as the schema.org point or contained within the specified bounding box.","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"]},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","geosparql:hasGeometry","geosparql:asWKT"],"required":true,"schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"]},{"path":["schema:spatialCoverage","geosparql:hasGeometry","geosparql:crs"],"description":"identifier string for coordinate reference system, e.g., 'CRS84'","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"]},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage"],"id":"http://schema.org/temporalCoverage","description":"Time period covered by the dataset. Can be ISO 8601 date ranges or structured temporal extent objects.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/temporalCoverage"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf"],"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"keyword":"anyOf"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","0"],"title":"a","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","0","time:intervalStartedBy"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalStartedBy","description":"identifier for a named time ordinal era that is older bound of time interval, e.g. 'isc:LowerDevonian' ","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalStartedBy"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","0","time:intervalFinishedBy"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalFinishedBy","description":"identifier for a named time ordinal era that is younger bound of time interval, e.g. 'isc:LowerDevonian' ","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalFinishedBy"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","1"],"title":"b","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","1","time:hasBeginning"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","1","time:hasBeginning","time:inTimePosition"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inTimePosition","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"ref":"0","effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inTimePosition"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","1","time:hasEnd"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","1","time:hasEnd","time:inTimePosition"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inTimePosition","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"ref":"0","effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inTimePosition"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","2"],"title":"c","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","2","time:hasBeginning"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"ref":"1","effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","_anyOf","2","time:hasEnd"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"ref":"1","effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd"},{"path":["schema:temporalCoverage","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","description":"free text description of the temporal extent. Declared here rather than in one interval form so that any object form below may carry it; the plain ISO 8601 string form cannot.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.temporalExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured"],"id":"http://schema.org/variableMeasured","description":"What the dataset measures (e.g. temperature, pressure).","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/variableMeasured"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"string label associated with the variable in the dataset serialization","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:alternateName"],"id":"http://schema.org/alternateName","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/alternateName"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:measurementTechnique"],"id":"http://schema.org/measurementTechnique","description":"Text description or URI specifying how values for the variable were obtained.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/measurementTechnique"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:propertyID"],"id":"http://schema.org/propertyID","description":"identifier or name for the property concept","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/propertyID"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:unitText"],"id":"http://schema.org/unitText","description":"unit of measurement as text","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/unitText"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:unitCode"],"id":"http://schema.org/unitCode","description":"URI or code identifying the unit of measure","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/unitCode"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:minValue"],"id":"http://schema.org/minValue","description":"minimum numeric value in the dataset","schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/minValue"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:maxValue"],"id":"http://schema.org/maxValue","description":"maximum numeric value in the dataset","schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/maxValue"},{"path":["schema:variableMeasured","schema:url"],"id":"http://schema.org/url","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.variableMeasured"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/url"},{"path":["schema:includedInDataCatalog"],"id":"http://schema.org/includedInDataCatalog","description":"The data catalog that contains this dataset. Object with @id, name, and url identifying the containing catalog.","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/includedInDataCatalog"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2"],"title":"a","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:narrower"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower","description":"Narrower (child) concepts in the hierarchy. Items are inline concept objects or @id references.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:broader"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader","description":"Broader (parent) concepts in the hierarchy. Items are inline concept objects or @id references.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:topConceptOf"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf","description":"Concept scheme(s) for which this is a top concept.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:inScheme"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme","description":"Concept scheme(s) this concept belongs to.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:editorialNote"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote","description":"Note for editors and maintainers.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:changeNote"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote","description":"Note documenting a change.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:historyNote"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote","description":"Note about past state or use.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:note"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note","description":"General note about this concept.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:scopeNote"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote","description":"Note clarifying meaning and/or intended use.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:definition"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition","description":"Formal explanation of the meaning of this concept.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:notation"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation","description":"Classification code for this concept within a scheme (a single notation string, consistent with CdifCodelistConcept).","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:prefLabel"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel","description":"Preferred lexical label for this concept. A single string, a single language-tagged value, or an array of language-tagged values. Each language should appear at most once.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:termCode"],"id":"http://schema.org/termCode","description":"A representative code for this keyword in the controlled vocabulary. Analogous to skos:Notation","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/termCode"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:inDefinedTermSet"],"id":"http://schema.org/inDefinedTermSet","description":"The controlled vocabulary responsible for this keyword, as EITHER a plain URI string identifying the vocabulary, OR an object reference ({\"@id\": \"<uri>\"}) to a vocabulary defined elsewhere in the document. Both forms are already in use across CDIF profiles and downstream ADA building blocks; permitting only the string form made the object form - the natural JSON-LD spelling of a reference - invalid, while this class's own union-type policy above explicitly anticipates both.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/inDefinedTermSet"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier"],"id":"http://schema.org/identifier","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/identifier"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:propertyID"],"id":"http://schema.org/propertyID","description":"In this context for the schema:PropertyValue, this field is an identifier for the identifier schema, e.g. DOI, ARK.  Get values from https://registry.identifiers.org/registry/ for interoperability. URI-shape values MUST be serialized as JSON-LD IRI references ({\"@id\":\"...\"}) so they participate in RDF entailment; free-label strings remain valid as strings.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/propertyID"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:value"],"id":"http://schema.org/value","description":"the identifier string. E.g. 10.5066/F7VX0DMQ","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/value"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:url"],"id":"http://schema.org/url","description":"web-resolveable string for the identifier; host name part is location of a resolver that will return some representation for the given identifier value. E.g. https://doi.org/10.5066/F7VX0DMQ ","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/url"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"text label for the term that is useful to human user","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:sameAs"],"id":"http://schema.org/sameAs","description":"other identifiers for the person","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/sameAs"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:contactPoint"],"id":"http://schema.org/contactPoint","description":"An email address or a contact web page (a form, an issue tracker), or both; at least one is required. Schema.org also allows telephone and postal contacts. A URL-only contact is ordinary in DCAT (a vcard:Kind with only vcard:hasURL), so requiring email made such records invalid.","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/contactPoint"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:contactPoint","schema:url"],"id":"http://schema.org/url","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/url"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:contactPoint","schema:email"],"id":"http://schema.org/email","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/email"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:affiliation"],"id":"http://schema.org/affiliation","description":"if affiliation is present, value must be a schema:Organization.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/affiliation"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:affiliation","schema:sameAs"],"id":"http://schema.org/sameAs","description":"other identifiers for the organization","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.organization"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/sameAs"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:affiliation","schema:identifier"],"id":"http://schema.org/identifier","description":"identifier for organization","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.organization"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/identifier"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:affiliation","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","description":"additional information about the agent or their relation to the described resource","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.organization"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:affiliation","schema:alternateName"],"id":"http://schema.org/alternateName","description":"other labels by which the organization might be known. A list when there are several; a single label may be a plain string, as JSON-LD framing writes a one-item list.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.organization"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/alternateName"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:affiliation","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"string label for organization that is meaningful for human users","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.organization"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:affiliation","schema:additionalType"],"id":"http://schema.org/additionalType","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.organization"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/additionalType"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:alternateName"],"id":"http://schema.org/alternateName","description":"other labels by which the person might be known. A list when there are several; a single label may be a plain string, as JSON-LD framing writes a one-item list.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/alternateName"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:identifier"],"id":"http://schema.org/identifier","description":"identifier for person, recommend ORCID","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/identifier"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","description":"additional information about the agent or their relation to the described resource","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","0","schema:provider","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"string label for person that is meaningful for human users, should format consistently. Recommend 'Family Name, Given name' format.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.person"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:termsOfService","dcterms:relation"],"id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation","description":"The related resource -- the DCAT canonical pointer to what is being related to, which is distinct from schema:url, the presentation URL of the link itself.\nAn @id reference is the RECOMMENDED form and a string is permitted, which is DCMI's own position: \"Recommended practice is to identify the related resource by means of a URI. If this is not possible or feasible, a string conforming to a formal identification system may be provided.\" DCMI declares no rdfs:range for this property, and of the 13 DCMI properties carrying an \"intended to be used with non-literal values\" restriction, this is deliberately not one. dcat.ttl does not re-declare or constrain it at all -- the only triple mentioning it in the whole DCAT vocabulary is `dcat:distribution rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation`.\nSo objectReference-only would be stricter than both DCAT and DCMI and would reject a form the specification sanctions. The anyOf matches how schema:additionalType is handled here: both forms valid, the object form used in examples and required only where a `contains` pins a specific value.\nIt was string-only until 2026-10-01, which rejected the @id form outright. Reported from outside by a PSDI validator taking a things-not-strings approach (profile-core#16): their DCAT catalogue mirrors the DCAT-3 spec examples and wrote {\"@id\": ...}, which failed both layers -- while CDIF's own documented URI serialization policy (agents.md) says URI values SHOULD be {\"@id\": ...}. The register required the one form its own policy argues against.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.labeledLink"],"effectiveId":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:termsOfService","dcat:hadRole"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#hadRole","description":"Role of the related resource. Present only on a link that expresses a relationship; a plain labeled link such as a license omits it.\nDCAT's declared range is dcat:Role (dcat.ttl: rdfs:range dcat:Role, and dcat:Role rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept), so the DCAT-native form is a node typed dcat:Role. That form was NOT accepted here before 2026-10-01: this property was cdifConceptOrTermOrString alone, which matches a bare string, a sealed @id reference, a schema:DefinedTerm or a skos:Concept -- none of which a dcat:Role-typed node satisfies, because JSON Schema does no subclass reasoning.\ndcat:Role is added as a branch rather than replacing the others, so the DCAT-native form becomes valid without invalidating anything already written. Note this leaves CDIF LOOSER than DCAT, deliberately: DCAT's range is dcat:Role alone, and CDIF also accepts a plain skos:Concept, a DefinedTerm, an @id reference and a string. That is the same both-forms stance taken on dcterms:relation, and it is a choice rather than an oversight -- do not read the extra branches as something not yet tightened.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.labeledLink"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#hadRole"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:termsOfService","schema:url"],"id":"http://schema.org/url","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.labeledLink"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/url"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:termsOfService","schema:description"],"id":"http://schema.org/description","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.labeledLink"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/description"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:termsOfService","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.labeledLink"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:distribution","_anyOf","1","schema:termsOfService","_then"],"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.labeledLink"],"keyword":"then"},{"path":["schema:includedInDataCatalog","schema:url"],"id":"http://schema.org/url","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/url"},{"path":["schema:includedInDataCatalog","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ecrr.bbr.metadata.ecrrProperties.ecrrDataset"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"}]}